  "description": "Change of use of an existing single-storey commercial unit (Use Class B8 – storage and distribution) to Use Class F1 (learning and non-residential institution) for operation as a community-focused tuition centre. The proposed use will provide after-school educational support in core subjects (Maths, English, Science) for local children aged 5–16. Minor internal alterations are proposed to create classrooms, a reception area, and staff facilities. No external alterations or extensions are planned. The tuition centre will operate at low intensity during weekday evenings (5pm–7pm) and weekend mornings (10am–12pm), with students arriving primarily on foot or by public transport. This proposal brings a currently vacant unit back into active use, supporting local educational needs in line with Newham’s community infrastructure policies.",
